# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit .env (rules #39/#40; .gitignore line 2).
#
# Exactly ONE secret is read by this project. Anything else living in .env is
# liability with no upside: it cannot help, it can only leak. If you find a
# variable here that no module reads, revoke it at its provider and delete the
# line - tests/unit/test_secrets_hygiene.py fails until you do.
#
# Placeholders below deliberately do NOT use real issuer prefixes, so the
# secret scanner can tell a template apart from a pasted key.

# Anthropic key for the verbal layer (config/<role>/game.toml -> [trash_talk]
# provider = "claude_api"). Read by infra/llm/claude_api.py::anthropic_key()
# and nothing else: the process environment wins, then this file (run games
# from the repo root, where .env lives). Optional: with provider = "template"
# (the zero-token default) the whole series plays without it, and the paid
# chain falls back to templates - and says so in the declaration - when absent.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<your-anthropic-key>

# --- Gmail is NOT configured here -------------------------------------------
# Reporting authenticates with OAuth 2.0 files, not an env var or a password:
#   credentials.json  the OAuth client downloaded from Google Cloud Console
#   token.json        minted on first consent; carries a NON-EXPIRING refresh
#                     token, so it is the most sensitive file in the checkout
# Both are git-ignored. Scope is gmail.send only (rule #30). See Appendix A,
# docs/PRD_reporting_gatekeeper.md, and docs/SECURITY.md for rotation.
#
# In particular there is no GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD: an app password bypasses 2FA and
# grants far more than sending. If you see one in a .env, revoke it.
